* table_churn.sno
* RTX-0c INSTRUMENT (s201) — a RELIABLE integer-keyed AGG benchmark.
* Bottleneck under test: rt_subscript_var (pattern_match.c:1000) — itoa the
* integer key, hash the resulting string, strcmp down the bucket chain, and
* mint a VCELL, because a subscript resolves to a NAME and never to a value.
* ⛔ MEASURE THIS PROGRAM WITH SCRIP_NOHUGE=1.  MEASURED s201, 10 runs each:
*   SCRIP_NOHUGE=1  454..508 ms  (1.12x spread)
*   default         367..2764 ms (7.5x spread, BIMODAL)
* &TIME is clock(), which is CPU time and charges SYSTEM time to the process,
* so the synchronous kernel compaction that gc_heap.c:149's MADV_HUGEPAGE can
* trigger lands directly inside the measured window.  That is an ENVIRONMENT
* hazard, not a property of this program: it inflates every SCRIP benchmark
* here, and it is the larger half of why table_access's A/B arms swap ranking.
* STABILITY IS BY CONSTRUCTION, and it is the entire point of the program:
*   (1) ONE table, created ONCE.  table_access.sno allocates a fresh
*       TABLE(512) 5,000 times, so its live set repeatedly grows and is
*       abandoned.  Even with SCRIP_NOHUGE=1 it still spreads 1.62x where
*       this program spreads 1.12x, so its shape is the SECOND cause.
*   (2) The working set (400) is BELOW 1000, so bench_sno_rtx.sh's scaler
*       cannot touch it — it only scales LT() literals >= 1000.  The pass
*       count is the single scalable literal, so auto-ranging adds PASSES
*       over a FIXED live set: live bytes constant, GC behaviour constant,
*       window linear in N.  That is what table_access cannot offer.
*   (3) NO pattern matching.  The 47 open crosscheck failures and both known
*       segvs (string_pattern, mixed_workload) are pattern-family; an AGG
*       instrument must not share a blast radius with them.
* Deterministic result: after P passes T<I> = I + P, so the checksum is
* SUM(1..400) + 400*P = 80200 + 400*P.  Feeds the harness's free ON/OFF
* output-identity gate, which is fatal on mismatch.
    &TRIM = 1
    &STLIMIT = 1000000000
    T = TABLE(1024)
    I = 0
FILL    I = LT(I, 400) I + 1                   :F(START)
    T<I> = I                                   :(FILL)
START   T1 = TIME()
    P = 0
PASS    P = LT(P, 10000) P + 1                 :F(DONE)
    I = 0
CELL    I = LT(I, 400) I + 1                   :F(PASS)
    T<I> = T<I> + 1                            :(CELL)
DONE    T2 = TIME()
    SUM = 0
    I = 0
SUMUP   I = LT(I, 400) I + 1                   :F(REPORT)
    SUM = SUM + T<I>                           :(SUMUP)
REPORT  OUTPUT = "result: " SUM
    OUTPUT = "ms: " (T2 - T1)
END
